   "thinking": "The features are coming out larger now, so the blur sums are inflating the magnitudes, and with \u03ba too small the densest template, 8, keeps winning. Raising \u03ba should counter that, though with blur a curved stroke or several nearby strokes can push values above 1. This sensitivity suggests the \u03ba calibration is the real problem, so I'm wondering whether the classification could be made less dependent on feature scale, perhaps through cosine similarity.\n\nCosine similarity would drop \u03ba entirely, but the input's overall scale would still shape confidence. I'll try \u03ba=0.6 first to see whether the blur actually helps before changing the classifier.\n\n",
